---
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import GlassWall from "../../components/clubhouse/GlassWall";

export const prerender = true;

export const title = "The Glass Wall";
export const navCategory = "clubhouse";
---

<Layout title="The Glass Wall - Matrix Hub">
  <div class="container mx-auto px-4 py-8">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-4 text-green-400">🧊 The Glass Wall</h1>
    <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 mb-4">
      The Clubhouse's transparency room. Most project sites ask you to
      trust their words; this room is built so you don't have to — it{' '}
      <strong class="text-gray-100">shows the workings, live</strong>, or
      says plainly when it can't.
    </p>
    <p class="text-gray-300 mb-6">
      Four panels: the receipts (claims that trace to a proof or to a read
      this page just made), the chain panel (MTX supply, the direct mint
      rate, minting status, and the casino reserve, read fresh from
      Polygon), the service status, and the crew log — what our automation
      runners actually did, published as summaries.
    </p>

    <!-- The room's one rule, stated up front. -->
    <div
      class="bg-green-900/40 border-2 border-green-500 rounded-lg p-4 mb-8 text-green-100"
    >
      <strong>The rule of this room:</strong> if a value can't be read, it
      shows as failed or unavailable — never backfilled with prose, never
      carried over from an earlier visit. A green tick here means something
      measured it, just now or in the latest published feed.
    </div>

    <GlassWall client:only="react" />

    <div class="mt-12 bg-gray-800 border border-gray-600 rounded-lg p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-green-400 mb-3">
        Where the facts come from
      </h2>
      <p class="text-gray-300 mb-3">
        The chain figures are read live from the same contracts the{' '}
        <a href="/security" class="text-green-400 hover:underline">
          /security
        </a>{' '}
        page publishes — the real MTX contract and the CasinoReserve —
        through the MTX Live Terminal's read path: keyless public Polygon
        endpoints with failover, an explicit failure state per figure, and
        nothing cached. The status panel is fed by Upptime monitors (open
        source, MIT) once HQ finishes wiring that feed; the crew log is
        published by our own runner tooling as summaries only. MTX is the
        utility token of the Matrix Hub ecosystem; nothing here is
        financial advice, and nothing here promises anything about price.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-300">
        Want to learn the checking skills yourself? The{' '}
        <a href="/proving-ground/" class="text-green-400 hover:underline">
          Proving Ground
        </a>{' '}
        teaches them hands-on — this room is where you come to watch them
        applied.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Built from the commons: what this page is actually built from. -->
    <div class="mt-8 bg-gray-800 border border-gray-600 rounded-lg p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-green-400 mb-3">
        Built from the commons
      </h2>
      <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">
        This room stands on open-source software, the way the whole site
        does:
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-300">
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/withastro/astro"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-green-400 hover:underline font-bold"
          >
            Astro
          </a>{' '}
          <span class="text-gray-400">(MIT)</span> — the static site framework
          this page is built and shipped with.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/facebook/react"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-green-400 hover:underline font-bold"
          >
            React
          </a>{' '}
          <span class="text-gray-400">(MIT)</span> — the interactive island
          the four panels run as.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/ethers-io/ethers.js"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-green-400 hover:underline font-bold"
          >
            ethers
          </a>{' '}
          <span class="text-gray-400">(MIT)</span> — the read-only contract
          calls behind the chain panel and the live receipts.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/tailwindlabs/tailwindcss"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-green-400 hover:underline font-bold"
          >
            Tailwind CSS
          </a>{' '}
          <span class="text-gray-400">(MIT)</span> — the styling, in the
          site's own theme. The receipt badges follow the{' '}
          <a
            href="https://github.com/badges/shields"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-green-400 hover:underline"
          >
            Shields
          </a>{' '}
          <span class="text-gray-400">(Apache-2.0)</span> badge pattern,
          rendered locally — no badge images are loaded from anywhere.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/CloudCannon/pagefind"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-green-400 hover:underline font-bold"
          >
            Pagefind
          </a>{' '}
          <span class="text-gray-400">(MIT)</span> — indexes this page into
          the site search at build time, no server involved.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-4">
        The panels themselves are hand-built for this room — no trackers,
        nothing loaded from a CDN.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
